review_comments:
It will not.

Most of the other `*Native` or `*Estimate` operations are element wise, so they can be implemented "recursively" via the scalar calls.

You need some path that was recursive or otherwise guaranteed that this handling would be identical to what the JIT does. In many cases that could likely be:
```csharp
#if MONO
    if (Vector128.IsHardwareAccelerated)
    {
        return ShuffleNative();
    }
#endif

    return Shuffle();
```

However, for some of the pre-AVX fallbacks where the JIT can't trivially implement it; something else would need to be figured out.
